# Cloudflare Pages reads this file automatically and sends these as real
# HTTP response headers. GitHub Pages ignores this file entirely (it has
# no way to send custom headers), so it does nothing until static hosting
# moves to Cloudflare Pages — see worker/README.md, "Move static hosting
# to Cloudflare Pages", for that cutover.
#
# frame-ancestors, Permissions-Policy, and blocking a stray wildcard
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin on HTML documents can only be done with a
# real header — a <meta http-equiv> CSP tag (already present on every
# page) can't express any of them.
#
# script-src is plain 'self' here — CSP Phase B (see git log) converted
# every page's inline <script> blocks and onclick= attributes to external
# .js files, so no page needs 'unsafe-inline' for scripts anymore. This
# used to say 'self' 'unsafe-inline' as a fallback for pages not yet
# converted; keeping it after Phase B finished meant every page got BOTH
# this header and its own stricter override in the same response —
# Cloudflare sends one Content-Security-Policy header per matching rule,
# and multiple matches all get sent, not just the most specific. Two
# headers didn't loosen anything in practice (browsers enforce the
# intersection), but it was pure noise. style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' —
# pages still use scattered style="" attributes and <style> blocks that
# weren't part of that pass.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.anjanpatel.ca; img-src 'self' data: https:; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'

# Page-specific overrides below still exist for real differences the
# general rule above can't express: connect-src (API-calling pages vs.
# the static legal pages) and flange's extra cdnjs.cloudflare.com in
# script-src. Every value here now matches what's in the page's own
# <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> tag.
